    "name": {
      "value": "Mask of Uncanny Breath"
    },
    "source": {
      "value": "tv"
    },
    "description": {
      "value": "A thin wooden mask carved in the shape of a skull, monstrous face, or eerily featureless visage, a mask of uncanny breath fully covers your face. While wearing it, each breath you take feels cool and pure, perfectly flowing to feed your ki. You gain resistance 10 to inhaled poisons and can breathe in an airless or toxic environment. When you breathe in, fragments of bizarre knowledge flow through you, granting you a +2 item bonus to Occultism checks.\n\n- **Activate:** Free Action\n- **Frequency:** once per day\n\nYou gain 1 Focus Point, which you can use only to cast an occult monk ki spell. If not used by the end of your turn, this Focus Point is lost.\n\n- **Activate:** Reaction\n- **Frequency:** once per day\n- **Trigger:** Your unarmed Strike hits a creature that breathes\n\nThe mask contorts and inhales, sucking breath from your target's lungs. The target falls unconscious but doesn't fall prone or drop what it's holding. It wakes up at the end of your turn if it hasn't been woken up already."
    },
